IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wills-dates`
IMPORT `wills-rules`

-- Wills Act 1997 (Vic) -- the questions of the PERSON WITH AN INTEREST IN A DECEASED PERSON'S WILL.
--
-- SEAT: the individual who, after a death (or while a relative lacks capacity), meets the Act from outside the will-maker's
-- chair: a beneficiary, the spouse, domestic partner, child or other relative, a person who would take on intestacy, or a
-- person applying for a Court-authorised will for someone without testamentary capacity. "Can the Court accept an unsigned
-- document as the will?", "Can the will be rectified, and by when must I apply?", "What becomes of a gift to someone who
-- died within 30 days?", "Was I the deceased's domestic partner?", "Can I see the will?". The Court, the Registrar and the
-- personal representative get no seat: their satisfactions and orders are asked as facts.
--
-- Every question takes plain facts (yes/no, numbers, dates, a choice from a list) and calls the rules of wills-rules.l4.
-- The one rule with a deadline (s 31(2)) is a DEONTIC rule run inside; no question takes a DEONTIC or an EVENT.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Wills Act 1997,
-- Version No. 036 (26 April 2021), not the authorised version. (c) State of Victoria; published with the authority of the
